// Behaviour names, canonicalised across the two languages.
//
// `implements_behaviour` stores whatever the module declared, rendered with
// `inspect/1`. An Elixir module writing `@behaviour GenServer` produces
// "GenServer"; an Erlang module writing `-behaviour(gen_server)` produces
// ":gen_server", colon and all, because that is how the atom inspects.
//
// A rule matching `implements_behaviour(mod, "GenServer")` therefore sees
// only the Elixir half. That is not a small half. On one project swept
// here, 100 modules declared `GenServer` and 42 declared `:gen_server` —
// roughly thirty percent of the gen_servers in the tree, all of them in
// dependencies, which is exactly where nobody is reading the source and a
// bug survives longest.
//
// The failure is silent in the worst way: the analysis returns fewer
// findings, not an error, and fewer findings is indistinguishable from
// cleaner code. It was found only by comparing a Datalog result against the
// raw extractor output that fed it.
//
// So rules should ask `behaves_as(mod, "GenServer")` rather than matching
// the declared string. The canonical name is the Elixir spelling, which is
// what the rules already say.

.decl behaviour_alias(declared: symbol, canonical: symbol)

behaviour_alias("GenServer", "GenServer").
behaviour_alias(":gen_server", "GenServer").
behaviour_alias("gen_server", "GenServer").

behaviour_alias("Supervisor", "Supervisor").
behaviour_alias(":supervisor", "Supervisor").
behaviour_alias("supervisor", "Supervisor").

behaviour_alias("GenStateMachine", "GenStateMachine").
behaviour_alias(":gen_statem", "GenStateMachine").
behaviour_alias("gen_statem", "GenStateMachine").

behaviour_alias("GenEvent", "GenEvent").
behaviour_alias(":gen_event", "GenEvent").
behaviour_alias("gen_event", "GenEvent").

behaviour_alias("Application", "Application").
behaviour_alias(":application", "Application").
behaviour_alias("application", "Application").

// Elixir-only behaviours. Listed so that `behaves_as` is total — a rule
// asking about one of these should not have to know whether it has an
// Erlang spelling.
behaviour_alias("GenStage", "GenStage").
behaviour_alias("Broadway", "Broadway").
behaviour_alias("Phoenix.LiveView", "Phoenix.LiveView").
behaviour_alias("Phoenix.Channel", "Phoenix.Channel").
behaviour_alias("Task", "Task").
behaviour_alias("Agent", "Agent").

// Wrappers that run a GenServer (or a gen_statem loop forwarding to
// GenServer-shaped callbacks) and hand their users the same init/1,
// handle_call/3, handle_cast/2, handle_info/2 contract. A module
// declaring one of these answers calls, blocks on receives and defers
// replies exactly as a GenServer does, and every rule about those
// callbacks applies. Postgrex's Notifications is a SimpleConnection;
// before this alias reply_contract and callback_receive could not see it.
behaviour_alias("Connection", "GenServer").
behaviour_alias("Postgrex.SimpleConnection", "GenServer").
behaviour_alias("Postgrex.ReplicationConnection", "GenServer").

.decl behaves_as(mod: symbol, canonical: symbol)

behaves_as(mod, canonical) :-
  implements_behaviour(mod, declared),
  behaviour_alias(declared, canonical).

// Anything not in the alias table passes through unchanged, so a rule can
// still ask about a behaviour nobody thought to list. Without this, adding
// the indirection would LOSE matches for every behaviour the table omits —
// turning a fix for under-reporting into a fresh source of it.
behaves_as(mod, declared) :-
  implements_behaviour(mod, declared),
  !behaviour_alias(declared, _).

// What a behaviour is, by the properties rules ask about. One table, three
// kinds: `loop` — the module runs a callback loop over its own mailbox, so
// a receive or a blocking call in a callback is on the server's stack;
// `gen_server_like` — handle_call/3 answers with GenServer's return
// contract, so `{:noreply, _}` is a deferred reply; `terminating` — the
// behaviour calls terminate/2,3 on the way down. Five analyses each kept
// their own list of the first kind and no two agreed.
.decl process_behaviour(canonical: symbol, kind: symbol)

process_behaviour("GenServer", "loop").
process_behaviour("GenStateMachine", "loop").
process_behaviour("GenEvent", "loop").
process_behaviour("GenStage", "loop").
process_behaviour("Broadway", "loop").
process_behaviour("Supervisor", "loop").
process_behaviour("Phoenix.LiveView", "loop").
process_behaviour("Phoenix.LiveComponent", "loop").
process_behaviour("Phoenix.Channel", "loop").

process_behaviour("GenServer", "gen_server_like").
process_behaviour("GenStage", "gen_server_like").

process_behaviour("GenServer", "terminating").
process_behaviour("GenStage", "terminating").
process_behaviour("GenStateMachine", "terminating").
process_behaviour("GenEvent", "terminating").
process_behaviour("Broadway", "terminating").
process_behaviour("Phoenix.LiveView", "terminating").
